Hangman Riddle Game

A terminal word-guessing game written in Python. Instead of guessing a hidden word letter by letter, you read a riddle-style clue and try to guess the word. Every wrong guess reveals one more letter, so the word slowly appears.

Features
Player login: new players enter a name and age, and returning players get a "Welcome back" message
Words grouped into categories (for example nature, object, concept)
Each word in a category is asked once, in random order
Wrong guesses reveal the next letter, with a limit of 6 tries per word
Score shown at the end of each game
Type quit at any time to stop and see your score
Input validation, so typing letters where a number is expected doesn't crash the game
How to run

You need Python 3 installed. There are no external libraries.

Download or clone this repository
Open a terminal in the project folder
Run:
python hangman.py
Project files
File	Purpose
hangman.py	The game
word.json	The words, clues and categories
players.json	Created automatically on first run, stores player names and ages (not uploaded to GitHub)
Adding your own words

Open word.json and add an entry in this format:

json
{
  "word": "Echo",
  "clue": "It cannot speak until spoken to, yet repeats what you say.",
  "category": "phenomenon"
}
What I used and practiced
Python functions, loops and conditions
Reading and writing JSON files
try/except for error handling
